# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Threshold signatures and multi-party computation, free of I/O"
description: """
A multi-party computation library for OCaml. The first protocol is FROST,
the two-round threshold Schnorr signature scheme of RFC 9591: distributed key
generation by trusted dealer or by the two-round Pedersen DKG, two-round
signing, signature-share verification with identifiable abort, and Shamir
secret sharing with Feldman verifiable secret sharing over an abstract
prime-order group.

The protocol core is a pure state machine: no I/O, no scheduler, no clock and
no ambient randomness. Time enters only as a timeout input the driver chooses
to inject and randomness only as a function the caller supplies, so the same
code drives a Unix process, a MirageOS/Solo5 unikernel, and a fully
deterministic in-memory simulator that replays an entire n-party run,
adversarial message schedule included, from a single 32-byte seed.

The FROST(Ed25519, SHA-512) ciphersuite depends on mirage-crypto-ec alone --
no zarith, hence no GMP -- and its signatures are ordinary RFC 8032 Ed25519
signatures, verifiable by any standard verifier."""
maintainer: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
authors: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
license: "ISC"
tags: [
  "mpc" "threshold-signatures" "tss" "frost" "schnorr" "ed25519" "org:mirage"
]
homepage: "https://github.com/reuna147/ocaml-mpc"
doc: "https://reuna147.github.io/ocaml-mpc/"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/reuna147/ocaml-mpc/issues"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14.0"}
  "dune" {>= "3.6" & >= "3.6"}
  "digestif" {>= "1.2.0"}
  "eqaf" {>= "0.9"}
  "mirage-crypto-ec" {>= "2.1.0"}
  "mirage-crypto-rng" {with-test & >= "2.1.0"}
  "alcotest" {with-test}
  "qcheck-core" {with-test}
  "qcheck-alcotest" {with-test}
  "ohex" {with-test & >= "0.2.0"}
  "yojson" {with-test & >= "2.0.0"}
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "subst"] {dev}
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/reuna147/ocaml-mpc.git"
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY -- delete this file before submitting to opam-repository.
#
# Mirage_crypto_ec.Ed25519.Primitive, and its scalar_*_into variants, are additions in
# the Reuna fork and are not yet upstream. Until they land, these pins let
# `opam install --deps-only --with-test .` resolve. Pinned by commit, never by branch:
# a moving branch would make a build unreproducible, and this is key-handling code.
#
# e6ed509 is on the fork's ec-into-and-x25519 branch. Repin once it reaches main.
pin-depends: [
  [ "mirage-crypto.2.4.0"     "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/mirage-crypto.git#main" ]
  [ "mirage-crypto-rng.2.4.0" "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/mirage-crypto.git#main" ]
  [ "mirage-crypto-ec.2.4.0"  "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/mirage-crypto.git#main" ]
]
